# LeakSanitizer suppressions (tools/run_asan.sh). Each entry says why.

# The Python interpreter behind CPA's leakage models is shut down with
# Py_FinalizeEx() at exit (LeakageModel::globalShutdown), but CPython and
# NumPy keep some module, type and interned-string memory for the life of the
# process by design. Our own reference counting (src/leakage_model.cpp) is
# balanced by hand; anything allocated inside the interpreter is its business.
leak:libpython3
leak:_multiarray_umath
